# The catalog cannot be read at all (the fake gateway's /models answers 503
# throughout), and `/model` is asked three times: once to read again (the
# launch read began well over a second ago, however slowly the binary
# started), once inside the second after that read began -- fx's cache starts
# no load then and opens the menu over the failure it holds (`beginLoad`,
# `model_cache_runtime.zig:441-442`; `openMenu`, `:529-539`) -- and once after
# that second. `modelsdelay 0` stamps the gateway log's catalog lines with when
# they were asked; the evidence is two catalog reads after the launch's, not
# three. Escape and the next `/` are 0.3 s apart: fx holds an Escape for
# 30 ms to see whether a key follows it (`main.zig:188`), and under load its
# loop can read both at once, as one chord, which types `model` into the
# menu's search rather than submitting the command -- the empty composer row
# in `inside-floor` is what says it was submitted.
models models.json
modelsdown
modelsdelay 0
wait 4
snap start
type /model
key Enter
wait 0.1
key Escape
wait 0.3
type /model
key Enter
wait 0.3
snap inside-floor
key Escape
wait 1.5
type /model
key Enter
wait 0.5
snap after-floor
gwlog
